{title: It Is Our Duty}
{subtitle: Ezra 10:28; 10:1–4; 10:10–12; 10:16–17}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Ezra wept before the house of God
A [Bb]large assembly [C]gathered a[Dm]round
Men and women weeping bitterly
[Bb]Sin had filled the [C]holy [Dm]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Sheca[Bb]niah spoke up to Ezra's [F]ear
[C]We have been unfaithful to [Dm]God
Yet [Bb]hope remains for Israel [Dm]now
Let us [Bb]follow the cove[Dm]nant
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Send away all these foreign [F]wives
A[C]long with their children [Dm]too
Do it according to the [F]Law
It [C]is our duty to [Dm]do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Ezra stood up and spoke aloud
[Bb]You have added [C]to Israel's [Dm]guilt
Make confession to the Lord your God
[Bb]Do his [C]will and sepa[Dm]rate
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Heads of families sat to judge
Ex[Bb]amining each [C]case with [Dm]care
From the sons of Bebai's line
Ath[Bb]lai a[C]greed to [Dm]leave
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Send away all these foreign [F]wives
A[C]long with their children [Dm]too
Do it according to the [F]Law
It is [C]our duty to do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]The matter was dealt with
[Bb]The [C]law was [Dm]kept
{end_of_verse}
